Compare extrusion, drawing, and sheet forming through flow, anisotropy, and failure evidence (@metal-extrusion-drawing-sheet: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metals-and-metallurgical-production, #source "../sources/Principles-of-Metal-Forming-NPTEL.lingua#r_7V0FT0Q67E19BFVTK57QABNPX8", #source "../sources/Aluminium-Automotive-Manual.lingua#r_73MPKA19MDBSQ96195B818Z49T", #source "../sources/Ferrous-Metals-Processing-BREF.lingua#r_49RSZE1MH5VHM49SDAXFQGHWRD", #metals-and-metallurgical-production "Recovery-recrystallization-grain-growth-and-texture-evolution.lingua#r_7988JVB7B2ER75AQKC9QVED6WQ", #materials-engineering "../../../engineering/materials-engineering/processing/Thermal-processing-quench-stress-and-microstructural-targets.lingua#r_4BKNXCFTWT0F434PM2ZP6V9GJQ") { r_78H51E21H22BGE65JJNHVR9ASE
**Read:** [Principles of Metal Forming Technology — Pradeep Kumar Jha, NPTEL](../sources/Principles-of-Metal-Forming-NPTEL.lingua#r_7V0FT0Q67E19BFVTK57QABNPX8), all extrusion, wire/tube drawing, sheet, instability, and defect material; [Aluminium Automotive Manual — European Aluminium and collaborators](../sources/Aluminium-Automotive-Manual.lingua#r_73MPKA19MDBSQ96195B818Z49T), the complete extrusion/rolled/forged product and forming/design cases used; [Ferrous Metals Processing Industry — European Commission BREF](../sources/Ferrous-Metals-Processing-BREF.lingua#r_49RSZE1MH5VHM49SDAXFQGHWRD), whole relevant wire/cold-rolling and intermediate-treatment chapters.

Extrusion, wire/tube drawing, and sheet operations create different contact, stress, strain, rate, and thermal fields. Tool geometry, friction, lubrication, prior structure, texture, hardening, thickness, and path can influence dimensional accuracy, surface, formability, and failure. A tensile elongation alone does not predict every forming limit.

Derive representative load/work and strain/geometry accounts before selecting an empirical relation or simulation. State the damage/localization or instability model and its calibration domain. Observations of thinning, earing, cracking, springback, or surface defects can have competing mechanical, thermal, structural, or tooling explanations.

Connect intermediate treatments and changing material state with the whole route. Repeated reductions, annealing, cooling, surface treatment, joining, and inspection affect final use. Production quality depends on feed variability and maintained tooling as well as nominal process settings.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete extrusion/drawing case and a sheet-forming case from full methods. Independently check strain, material/work, and a significant load or instability calculation. Compare two model/process assumptions against independent geometry/strain/property observations. Investigate one defect with discriminating evidence and defend a route meeting a specified function under realistic variability. Dedicated manufacturing/machine-design trails deepen tools and production equipment while reusing these metallurgical principles.

**Continue:** [Test restoration and grain evolution through thermal, deformation, and structural histories](Recovery-recrystallization-grain-growth-and-texture-evolution.lingua#r_7988JVB7B2ER75AQKC9QVED6WQ).

